  failure"`) — same `vi.doMock("../src/index.ts", ...)` technique still applies through the new
  `scaffoldWithSpinner`/`resolveScaffoldTarget` composition.

**[packages/create-pantoken-app/tests/index.test.ts](packages/create-pantoken-app/tests/index.test.ts)**:

- Keep all existing tests' intent (`--help`, unknown platform, `--dir` scaffold, `html` alias) — the bin's
  black-box surface (`<platform> [--dir]`) is unchanged.
- Update its "vp install"-style assertion the same way as above (explicit `env.npm_config_user_agent`).
- Add one new test: `--yes` with no platform exits non-zero with a clear message.

**New file `ai/pantoken-ai/tests/cli.test.ts`** (no prior CLI tests exist to preserve):

- `pantoken-ai --help` lists both `init` and `scaffold` subcommands.
- `pantoken-ai init --tool cursor --dir <tmp>` writes the expected asset.
- `pantoken-ai init --tool bogus` exits non-zero (commander's `Option.choices()` validation).
